    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d578">

                <pb facs="0655" n="397" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg397"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115G95/15</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-17T15:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 17, 1915, 3 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 2.45 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2105. Your 1529, May 8, and my May 10.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d578-f1"/> Captain
                    Smith of S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Gulflight</hi>, states that the
                    conversation between the late Captain Gunter of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gulflight</hi> and the skipper of British patrol boat <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Filey</hi> was to the effect that Captain Gunter, in
                    replying that the ship was bound to Rouen, asked when he could secure a French
                    pilot. The reply of the patrol boat was that he could not get one there and
                    directed the <hi rendition="#italic">Gulflight</hi> to follow the patrols to the
                    Bishop Rock.</p>
                <p>The British Admiralty states in reply to my inquiry that the ships which did the
                    convoying are now at sea out of communication, but the details will be obtained
                    as soon as they return to port.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
